I had an IRC discussion about this a while ago.

I was told that the alt-key can't be used via terminal because the way
Nethack uses the keyboard (even when your terminal supports it - a lot of
terminal programs under windows don't pass ALT to the terminal, however,
puTTy is not one of these, IIRC).

So the only solution is to use the #chat, #dip, #adjust etc. commands -
they are a bit slower, but you'll get used to them in no time.

However, just recently I have noticed that certain ALT+key -combinations
DO have strange effects on hal.pp.fishpoo.fi or antisymmetric.com, so
perhaps it's not Nethack's code's fault, but the servers are just
configured strangely - 

try the following combinations:

ALT+8 ('[' on finnis keyb.), 
ALT+9 (']'), 
ALT+E (is interpreted as $, i.e. ALT+4), 
ALT+D ("    "   "     "  =ALT+P=pray, on antisymmetric)

... and various others. 

And also, one IS able to throw or drop $ (i.e. gold pieces) even on a
Finnish keyboard, where $ can be found under ALT+4.


So it seems to me the servers are just configured really weird.


